On November 17, 2026, a military transport aircraft, An-12, belonging to the Russian Aerospace Forces crashed near Kemerovo.
17 military personnel were killed.
Crew:
• Captain: M.G. Abuladze;
• First Officer: D.V. Nazarenko;
• Navigator: I.A. Gorshkov;
• Senior Radio Operator: I.V. Korovaev;
• Senior Flight Technician: I.N. Shevelev;
• Technician: A.K. Sinitsyn
This comes as 7 pilots of a Mi-8, Ka-52, and an SU fighter jet crashed and destroyed in friendly fire during drone interception mission, also less than a month ago a Russian Tu-95MS strategic bomber also crashed and killing everyone on board approximately 8 highly trained pilots and coordinators for ballistic air-launched missiles. All these losses in less than few months.

🇦🇱🇺🇸⚡️ — The U.S. State Department has approved a possible $210 million Foreign Military Sale (FMS) to Albania for two M142 High Mobility Artillery Rocket Systems (HIMARS).
The proposed package includes:
• 2 × M142 HIMARS launchers;
• 6 × M31A2 Guided Multiple Launch Rocket System (GMLRS) Unitary Pods;
• 6 × M30A2 GMLRS Alternative Warhead (AW) Pods;
• 8 × International Field Artillery Tactical Data Systems (IFATDS);
• 2 × M1152A1 High Mobility Multipurpose Wheeled Vehicles (HMMWVs);
• Associated communications equipment, support vehicles, spare parts, maintenance equipment, training and logistical support.
Albania will finance the purchase using Foreign Military Financing (FMF) loan funds.
